git diff <a> <b> compares two commits. - A diff is git's report of what changed between two versions of a file: old lines are marked as removed, new lines are marked as added.
Ex: git diff 3f2a91c 9b1f4c2
HEAD~1, HEAD~2 name commits counting back from HEAD.

